# The transpiler tokenizer's strict xfail list (tests/test_syntax_tokenize.rs;
# docs/research/transpiler-architecture.md §5, phase 1).
#
#   <input-set>/<relpath> <check> <reason>
#
# <check> is `lines` (the statements rebuilt from tokens differ from today's
# logical lines) or `numbers` (a number token's value differs from today's).
# An unlisted difference fails, and so does a listed line that no longer
# differs (XPASS): delete it then. Each reason names today's bug, with the
# manual or ngspice run that shows it.

# Phase 2b (Lexicon::join, Join::Parens): a Spectre statement whose
# parentheses are open at its line's end runs on into the next line in the
# tokens, as Spectre reads it (Reference 19.1 p.491, `if` conditions over
# lines); today's line stage keeps two lines and its card grammar joined
# them. Not a bug either side: the join moved from the cards to the tokens.
fixtures/tests/fixtures/conditionals/kit.scs lines the open-paren join is in the tokens now, not in the card stage
